  "statement": {
    "content": "$x$ قيس زاوية حادة حيث: $\\sin x = \\dfrac{1}{3}$ ."
  },
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "step": "01",
      "statement": "بيّن أن: $\\cos x = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}$ .",
      "learningPoints": [
        {
          "code": "4am_alaqat-muthallathiya_P2",
          "role": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "cognitiveDemand": "reason",
      "answerType": "selfCheck",
      "answerFormat": "اكتب برهانك هنا، ثم اضغط «سجّل إجابتي» لتطّلع على الحل النموذجي.",
      "hints": [
        {
          "id": "h1",
          "type": "look",
          "content": "العلاقة التي تربط جيب الزاوية وجيب تمامها هي $\\cos^2 x + \\sin^2 x = 1$ ."
        },
        {
          "id": "h2",
          "type": "direction",
          "content": "اعزل $\\cos^2 x$ ثم عوّض الجيب بقيمته، ولا تنس تربيع البسط والمقام معا."
        },
        {
          "id": "h3",
          "type": "strategy",
          "content": "$\\cos x$ عدد موجب تماما: خذ الجذر التربيعي الموجب."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$\\cos^2 x = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{9} = \\dfrac{8}{9}$ و $\\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}$ .",
        "incorrect": "قارن برهانك بالحل النموذجي سطرا سطرا، ثم قيّم إجابتك."
      },
      "solution": {
        "lines": [
          "$\\cos^2 x + \\sin^2 x = 1$ ، إذن $\\cos^2 x = 1 - \\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right)^2 = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{9} = \\dfrac{8}{9}$",
          "$\\cos x$ عدد موجب، إذن $\\cos x = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{9}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{4 \\times 2}}{3} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}$"
        ]
      },
      "timeSeconds": 180
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "step": "02",
      "statement": "ليكن العدد $B = 6\\sqrt{2} \\times \\cos x$ . بيّن أن $B$ عدد طبيعي.",
      "learningPoints": [
        {
          "code": "4am_alaqat-muthallathiya_P2",
          "role": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "cognitiveDemand": "apply",
      "answerType": "rational",
      "answerFormat": "اكتب قيمة $B$ (عدد طبيعي)",
      "expectedAnswer": "8",
      "hints": [
        {
          "id": "h1",
          "type": "look",
          "content": "عوّض $\\cos x$ بالكتابة المعطاة في السؤال 01."
        },
        {
          "id": "h2",
          "type": "direction",
          "content": "$\\sqrt{2} \\times \\sqrt{2} = 2$ ."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$B = 6\\sqrt{2} \\times \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} = \\dfrac{12 \\times 2}{3} = 8$ .",
        "incorrect": "عوّض ثم استعمل $(\\sqrt{2})^2 = 2$ واختزل."
      },
      "solution": {
        "lines": [
          "$B = 6\\sqrt{2} \\times \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} = \\dfrac{12 \\times (\\sqrt{2})^2}{3} = \\dfrac{12 \\times 2}{3}$",
          "$B = 8$ وهو عدد طبيعي."
        ],
        "result": "B = 8"
      },
      "work": "optional",
      "timeSeconds": 150
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "step": "03",
      "statement": "اكتب $\\tan x$ على الشكل $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{a}$ حيث $a$ عدد طبيعي.",
      "learningPoints": [
        {
          "code": "4am_alaqat-muthallathiya_P2",
          "role": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "cognitiveDemand": "apply",
      "answerType": "rational",
      "answerFormat": "اكتب العدد $a$ فقط (عدد طبيعي)",
      "expectedAnswer": "4",
      "hints": [
        {
          "id": "h1",
          "type": "look",
          "content": "$\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$ ."
        },
        {
          "id": "h2",
          "type": "direction",
          "content": "بعد القسمة اجعل المقام عددا ناطقا بضرب البسط والمقام في $\\sqrt{2}$ ."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$\\tan x = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{3}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}$ .",
        "incorrect": "اقسم الجيب على جيب التمام، ثم اجعل المقام عددا ناطقا."
      },
      "solution": {
        "lines": [
          "$\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\div \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}$",
          "$\\tan x = \\dfrac{1 \\times \\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2} \\times \\sqrt{2}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}$"
        ],
        "result": "\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"
      },
      "work": "optional",
      "timeSeconds": 150
    }
